Mutarataza ("the Licensor"). By installing, activating or using Vaultkit (the
"Software") you accept it. If you do not accept it, do not use the Software.

1. What you may do

1.1 Trial. When you first run the Software you receive a trial of fourteen (14)
    days with every feature enabled, at no charge and without giving payment
    details. One trial per machine. Attempting to obtain further trials by
    resetting, reinstalling or altering stored trial state is a breach of this
    Agreement.

1.2 Subscription. On payment of the applicable fee the Licensor grants you a
    non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the
    Software for the paid term, on up to three (3) Macs that you own or
    primarily control, for your own work. The licence lasts only as long as the
    subscription is paid and current.

1.3 Organisations. A licence bought by an organisation covers named individuals,
    not shared credentials; each individual needs their own licence. Contact the
    Licensor for volume terms.

2. What you may not do

You may not, and may not permit anyone else to:

  (a) copy, publish, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or otherwise distribute the
      Software or any part of it;
  (b) share, publish or resell a licence key, or use one on more machines than
      clause 1.2 allows;
  (c) modify, translate or create derivative works of the Software;
  (d) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except exactly so
      far as applicable law expressly permits despite this restriction (in the
      European Union, this includes the interoperability rights under Article 6
      of Directive 2009/24/EC, and nothing here limits rights that law declares
      cannot be excluded);
  (e) circumvent, disable or tamper with the licensing, trial or activation
      mechanisms, or use a key obtained by fraud or chargeback;
  (f) remove or obscure any copyright, trademark or licence notice.

Security research on the Software is welcome and is not restricted by clause
2(d); see SECURITY.md for how to report what you find.

3. Your data stays yours

The Software runs locally. The Licensor claims no right in your code, your keys,
your vaults or their contents, and has no access to them. What the Software does
send, and why, is stated in PRIVACY.md, which forms part of this Agreement.

4. Activation

The Software contacts the Licensor's licensing service to activate a key and
periodically to confirm the subscription is still current. It sends only what
PRIVACY.md lists. If the Software cannot reach the service, it continues to work
on the last confirmed entitlement for a grace period; after that it falls back to
the reduced mode described in clause 6.

5. Payment, renewal and cancellation

5.1 The subscription is annual and renews automatically at the then-current price
    until cancelled. You may cancel at any time, effective at the end of the paid
    term; the Software keeps working until that date.

5.2 Fees are stated at purchase and are exclusive of any tax the Licensor is
    required to add.

5.3 Refunds: within thirty (30) days of a first purchase, for any reason, on
    request. Renewals are refundable only where law requires it. Consumers in
    jurisdictions granting statutory withdrawal rights keep those rights in full.

6. What happens when a licence ends

When a trial expires, or a subscription lapses or is cancelled, the Software
enters a reduced mode. In that mode it will always let you see the state of your
system and mount, eject and remove your own vaults and organisations. The
Licensor will not withhold access to your own encrypted data behind a payment,
ever, and the Software stores nothing that a licence is needed to read: the
configuration it manages lives in your own ~/.gitconfig, ~/.ssh and APFS
volumes, and keeps working whether or not Vaultkit is installed.

7. Updates

The subscription includes all updates published during its term. Updates are
provided under this Agreement unless one ships with its own terms.

